      "block_id": "2605.00224_p9_b0",
      "text": "TUR-DPO: Topology- and Uncertainty-Aware Direct Preference Optimization\n",
      "bbox": [
        149.03,
        47.23,
        447.56,
        56.19
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        596,
        188,
        1790,
        224
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 8.97,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 71,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p9_b1",
      "text": "that require intensive reasoning. Our method adds structural\ntopology and calibrated uncertainty to the training goal.\nThis leads to models that are not only more accurate, but\nalso clearer about how they come to their conclusions.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.13,
        69.54,
        291.18,
        115.3
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        220,
        278,
        1164,
        461
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.86,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 231,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p9_b2",
      "text": "The primary positive impact that could come from this work\nis that language models will be more reliable and trust-\nworthy when it comes to tasks like answering questions,\nsummarizing, and having conversations. Focusing on how\nanswers are reached instead of just their final form might\nalso lead to more understandable and stable model behavior.\nAlso, the proposed training method\u2019s simplicity could make\nit easier to reproduce and build on alignment research.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.08,
        123.34,
        291.19,
        216.92
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        220,
        493,
        1164,
        867
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.86,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 460,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p9_b3",
      "text": "But there are still some ethical issues to think about. Be-\ncause TUR-DPO uses elicited topologies, any biases that\nare already in the parsers or the preference data may get\nworse during alignment. If the structural rewards are based\non bad or culturally biased logic, the model could become\n\u201dconfidently wrong,\u201d giving wrong information through a\n",
      "bbox": [
        54.12,
        224.81,
        291.09,
        294.65
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        216,
        899,
        1164,
        1178
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.06,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 347,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p9_b4",
      "text": "reasoning structure that seems to make sense. So, we advise\nagainst using models trained this way in situations where\nsafety is important, like medical diagnosis or legal advice,\nwhere logical mistakes can have serious real-world effects.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.08,
        296.69,
        290.68,
        342.44
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        220,
        1186,
        1162,
        1369
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.86,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 238,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p9_b5",
      "text": "This paper ultimately helps with the bigger goal of mak-\ning machine learning systems that better understand what\npeople want. It doesn\u2019t get rid of the risks that come with\nusing LLMs, like the chance of misuse or spreading false\ninformation, but it does give you tools to make these models\nmore logically sound and easier to understand.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.13,
        350.34,
        291.09,
        420.15
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        220,
        1401,
        1164,
        1680
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.06,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 338,
      "block_type": 0
    },
